WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:02.068
-This is very exciting.

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:03.569
You guys have a new talk show.
I can't wait.

00:00:03.569 --> 00:00:05.371
One of the things you've said
is you don't want guests

00:00:05.371 --> 00:00:07.173
who are just on
to promote their project.

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:08.807
-That's right.
-I would like to note

00:00:08.807 --> 00:00:11.110
you are on my show right now
promoting your project.

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:13.413
-That is true. But as a --
Listen, as a father --

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:16.015
-The answer to that
is we are hypocrites.

00:00:16.015 --> 00:00:18.617
-And also, as a father, I will
say, "Do as I say, not as I do."

00:00:18.617 --> 00:00:20.453
-Okay. Gotcha.
-I mean, just 'cause we're

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:22.655
in the pocket of big tobacco
doesn't mean that we sold out.

00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:24.390
-Oh, you've already sold out
to big tobacco?

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:25.525
-Yeah, bro. Phillip Morris --

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:26.993
-Kids, keep smoking
those Juul pods.

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:28.461
-You know what I'm saying?
Juuls, bro!

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:30.296
Can't be cool without a Juul!

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:33.333
-Bing!
-Very exciting. You have --

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:36.136
Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez
is on your show.

00:00:36.136 --> 00:00:38.371
Also from the Bronx,
which is really exciting.

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:41.674
And you went down to D.C. and
shot a little with her there.

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:42.975
You went and visited her there.

00:00:42.975 --> 00:00:44.576
How was it being with someone

00:00:44.576 --> 00:00:47.280
from the same place as you
in D.C.?

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.882
-Well, the wild part
about that was apparently

00:00:49.882 --> 00:00:51.818
the Capitol Police
do not have a sense of humor.

00:00:51.818 --> 00:00:53.753
-Okay.
-You can't just be walking down

00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:55.922
to the White House, be like,
"Yerr," and not get shot.

00:00:55.922 --> 00:00:58.324
So we had to tone that down
a little bit.

00:00:58.324 --> 00:01:00.093
-There was a lot of,
"Uh, do you have permits?

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:02.929
Do you have a permit to be here?
Do you have a permit
to shoot here, sir?"

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:05.398
-Also, I don't know if you've
noticed, since, you know,
we've upgraded the networks,

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:07.700
my man's got a little heavy
with the jewelry.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.802
-Had to go through
the metal detector six times.

00:01:09.802 --> 00:01:13.305
-No. Did you feel
like the Capitol

00:01:13.305 --> 00:01:16.209
had changed Ocasio-Cortez,
or did you feel like

00:01:16.209 --> 00:01:18.177
you guys brought the Bronx
out of her when you were there?

00:01:18.177 --> 00:01:19.345
-We definitely did.

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:20.613
-Definitely brought the Bronx
out of her.

00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:22.215
She just leaned out of her
office door and delivered

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:23.950
the heartiest "Yerr"
I've ever heard.

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:25.819
You know what I'm saying?
-Did other people --

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:27.486
Because those are
pretty close quarters.

00:01:27.486 --> 00:01:29.556
Were other people
in the Capitol a little --

00:01:29.556 --> 00:01:31.324
Could they tell
you guys were there?

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:33.492
-Well, what's funny -- I did not
know if most people know this.

00:01:33.492 --> 00:01:35.795
Mike Pence has a brother
that's a representative.

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:38.130
And surprisingly, we're filming
in front of his office,

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:40.099
and all of a sudden,
the Capitol Police comes

00:01:40.099 --> 00:01:41.667
and asks us for a film permit.

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:43.135
-Yeah. I wonder why.
-Really?

00:01:43.135 --> 00:01:45.137
-Hmm. Ya snitch.
-He's like,

00:01:45.137 --> 00:01:48.374
"Desus and Mero are here.
They're gonna slander me.

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:49.843
-"Hey, Mike, they're here.
Tell Mama."

00:01:49.843 --> 00:01:52.645
-Tell Mother.
Tell Mother to call."

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:54.347
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:56.583
-There is so much --
-Shout-out to nepotism.

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:58.317
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.317 --> 00:02:00.953
-There's some -- You know,
there is some criticism

00:02:00.953 --> 00:02:02.855
from within the halls
of Congress

00:02:02.855 --> 00:02:05.892
that, you know, Ocasio-Cortez
is shaking things up.

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:09.128
Did you feel that? Do you feel
like she's having an impact?

00:02:09.128 --> 00:02:12.031
-You know what it is? It's
because Congress is just so old.

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:13.766
It's, like, antiquated
old rules, stodgy.

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:16.169
-Stodgy old dudes.
-And then you got a New Yorker.

00:02:16.169 --> 00:02:17.503
And you know us New Yorkers.

00:02:17.503 --> 00:02:18.872
We like to be very frank
and very straight,

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:20.272
so they're not used to her.

00:02:20.272 --> 00:02:21.607
She's a little rough
around the edges,

00:02:21.607 --> 00:02:22.942
but I think she's
getting stuff done,

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:24.310
and it's making them
a little nervous.

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:25.678
-One of the things that...

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:29.115
[ Cheers and applause ]
She was working on --

00:02:29.115 --> 00:02:30.816
You know, she was not a fan
of the Amazon deal.

00:02:30.816 --> 00:02:32.952
Amazon has now pulled out.
How do you guys feel about

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:34.787
Amazon pulling out
of this New York deal?

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:36.923
-When you say "pull out,"
it's triggering for me,

00:02:36.923 --> 00:02:38.224
'cause I have four children.

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:39.492
-Okay. Gotcha.

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:40.793
-He's thinking a whole different
type of pulling out.

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:41.927
-I apologize.

00:02:41.927 --> 00:02:43.262
-I was like,
"What do you mean by that?"

00:02:43.262 --> 00:02:46.299
-Withdrawn. Withdrawn.
-Thank you, thank you.

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:48.401
-I'm not mad at them
pulling out the Amazon deal.

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:50.136
And it's not, like,
because I love New York

00:02:50.136 --> 00:02:52.371
and I'm worried about, like,
the culture and the community.

00:02:52.371 --> 00:02:53.540
Jeff Bezos has too much money,

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:55.141
and I'd like to see him
take the L.

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:56.442
-Okay, gotcha.
-Humble him.

00:02:56.442 --> 00:02:58.711
Listen.
You got $133 billion, man.

00:02:58.711 --> 00:03:00.313
Relax.
-$170.

00:03:00.313 --> 00:03:01.847
-Oh, wow. It's up to that now?

00:03:01.847 --> 00:03:04.049
-It is up to that by
the last time you Googled it.

00:03:04.049 --> 00:03:06.786
-Exactly. We don't need
another Amazon Center.

00:03:06.786 --> 00:03:08.554
New York is crowded enough
as it is.

00:03:08.554 --> 00:03:09.888
-Yeah.
-You know.

00:03:09.888 --> 00:03:11.757
It bothered me, though,
because I like Amazon Prime.

00:03:11.757 --> 00:03:13.125
Like, I just ordered
a panini maker

00:03:13.125 --> 00:03:14.827
at 2:00 last night
for some reason.

00:03:14.827 --> 00:03:16.929
But I can get around that.
-Okay. You can make it work.

00:03:16.929 --> 00:03:19.798
-I ordered like four air
purifiers. I don't know why.

00:03:19.798 --> 00:03:22.334
-They're like,
"Do you want them on Thursday?"

00:03:22.334 --> 00:03:23.536
You're like, "Hell yes."

00:03:23.536 --> 00:03:25.004
-I was like,
"Do I want a strawberry holder?

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:26.305
Of course I want
a strawberry holder."

00:03:26.305 --> 00:03:27.707
-And I'm not waiting
until Monday for it.

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:29.409
-[Bleep] that.

